Control Center: colour-coded sections, and adding, moving and renaming
entries and sections from the Control Center itself.

Section colours: each group gets a colour from its family (the part of its
name before " - ", e.g. "Graphics - Vector" -> Graphics). "Headers" colours
the section headers and adds a matching stripe to each sidebar group; "Whole
block" also tints each section from its header down to the next one; "Off"
looks as before. The choice is made in the "Section colours" box under the
search field and saved to ~/.config/yast-on-arch/section-colors.ini, where
colours can also be changed. A new genre gets the hue furthest from every
colour in use, saved to that file. A renamed section keeps its colour.
Each "More - System - <category>" section has a colour of its own: the
ones that match a family use it (Networking -> Network, Security & Accounts
-> Security, Hardware & Drivers -> Hardware, Gaming Helpers -> Games, System
Info & Monitors -> Information, Other -> Utilities), the others have
hand-picked colours. An [Aliases] section in the same file (Group name=
Family) puts any group, these included, into another family.

Layout: ~/.local/share/yast-on-arch/layout.ini ([Moves] file.desktop=GROUP,
[Names] GROUP=Name) shows an entry in another section or a section under
another name, without changing the installed .desktop files. An entry moved
into a section that no longer exists is shown in its own section again.

"Add or change..." button (and right-click on a program -> "Move to another
section..."): a dialog to add a program, add a section, move a program and
rename a section. It runs the same "yast add-app / add-section / move-app /
rename-section" commands as the terminal (through $YAST_LAUNCHER) and
restarts the Control Center to show the change.

Applies on top of patches 07, 20 and 21.

